# PR review — orchestration protocol

Coordinates specialized review subagents (via the Agent tool) and consolidates their
findings into one summary. Each subagent loads the **domain skill** that governs the files
it touches — this skill does not duplicate that content.

## Step 1 — Initialize

1. Get the PR number from context, or ask the user.
{% if git_host == "github" -%}
2. Identify the repo: `gh repo view --json nameWithOwner -q .nameWithOwner`.
3. Fetch the diff: `gh pr diff {PR}`.
4. Load existing inline comments (`gh api repos/{REPO}/pulls/{PR}/comments`) into a
   `{path, line}` set to avoid reposting.
5. Read PR intent: `gh pr view {PR} --json title,body,headRefName`.
6. Get the head SHA: `gh pr view {PR} --json headRefOid -q .headRefOid`.
{%- else -%}
2. Fetch the diff and the PR metadata (title, body, head branch, head SHA) via your git
   host's CLI or API.
3. Load existing inline comments into a `{path, line}` set to avoid reposting.
{%- endif %}
{% if issue_tracker != "none" %}7. Extract the tracker key from the branch name (pattern `{{ issue_prefix }}-[0-9]+`).{% endif %}

## Step 2 — Launch subagents in parallel

Send **one message** with all subagent calls (Agent tool) — simultaneous. Pass each one
the repo, PR number, diff, existing comments, PR intent, and head SHA. When all complete,
run Step 3.

## Severity labels (all subagents)

- 🚨 **Critical** — bugs or logic errors that will cause failures.
- 🔒 **Security** — vulnerabilities or data exposure.
- ⚠️ **Warning** — code smells or maintainability problems.
- 💡 **Suggestion** — optional improvements.

## Universal rules (every subagent)

1. **Comment only on added lines** — diff lines starting with `+` (excluding `+++`).
2. **Skip duplicates** — if a `{path, line}` within ±3 lines already has a comment, skip.
3. **Mark resolved** — reply `[RESOLVED] Appears fixed by recent changes.` on existing
   comments whose problem is now fixed.
4. **≥ 80% confidence** — report only when confident; skip when unsure.
5. **One positive highlight** before listing problems.
6. **Tone:** specific, actionable, collegial — explain *why* it's a problem.
7. **Never** approve, request-changes, or modify files — comment only.
8. **Marker:** start every inline comment with `<!-- ai-review:{type} -->` (invisible in
   rendered view), so consolidation can parse it.

Prefer the GitHub MCP (`pull_request_review_write`) for posting; {% if git_host == "github" %}fall back to `gh api
repos/{REPO}/pulls/{PR}/comments` with `commit_id`, `path`, `line`{% else %}otherwise use your host's review API{% endif %}.

---

## Subagent 1 — Security
**Marker:** `<!-- ai-review:security -->`

Load any domain skill whose trigger covers security/auth files. Review the diff for:
secrets or service credentials leaking to client code; endpoints missing the project's
auth/authorization gate; missing input validation before data access; injection;
overly-permissive access rules (multi-tenant isolation removed); unsafe headers/CORS.

**Second pass:** re-read the full diff, list every uncommented file, and for each ask "does
this violate a security rule?" Skip only when you can say explicitly why it's clean.

## Subagent 2 — Requirements & Definition of Done
**Marker:** `<!-- ai-review:requirements -->` · posts **one PR-level comment** (no inline).

{% if issue_tracker != "none" -%}
**Track A — tracker issue:** extract the key (`{{ issue_prefix }}-N`) from the branch;
fetch its title, description, and acceptance criteria.
**Track B — spec files:** check `.forge/specs/<slug>/` (spec.md, plan.md, tasks) and the PR
body for spec references.
Merge whatever has content; note the source of each item. If neither exists, post
"⚠️ No tracker issue or spec found — requirements check skipped." and stop.
{%- else -%}
Read the PR body and any `.forge/specs/<slug>/` artifacts (spec.md, plan.md, tasks) for
the intended behavior. If none exist, post "⚠️ No spec found — requirements check skipped."
and stop.
{%- endif %}

Assess each acceptance criterion against the diff: ✅ implemented, ❌ missing, 🔲 in the
Definition of Done but unverified.

## Subagent 3 — Test coverage
**Marker:** `<!-- ai-review:testing -->`

Load the project's testing domain skill (if any). Flag: new public surface (endpoint,
module) with no corresponding test; modified unit with a previously-existing test now gone;
mock anti-patterns; weakened assertions; missing error-path coverage.

**Second pass:** list each new/modified unit with no test and ask "is there coverage for
the happy path + at least one error case?" Skip only with explicit justification.

## Subagent 4 — Architecture & conventions
**Marker:** `<!-- ai-review:architecture -->`

**Phase 0:** load `AGENTS.md` (anti-patterns, conventions) and every domain skill whose
trigger path matches a file in the diff.
**Phase 1:** extract the explicit rules and anti-patterns from those documents into a
matrix.
**Phase 2:** evaluate each file against each applicable rule — PASS / VIOLATION / N/A. N/A
only when a rule is structurally inapplicable to that file type.

**Second pass:** list unevaluated files and re-apply the matrix. Cite the violating line and
the source rule in each comment.

## Subagent 5 — Regression & hallucination
**Marker:** `<!-- ai-review:regression -->`

Review for changes unrelated to the PR's goal or signs of AI-generated artifacts:
unrelated deletions, phantom imports of symbols that don't exist, wrong-signature calls,
leftover `TODO`s, type assertions hiding compiler errors, duplicated logic that already
exists, weakened error handling or test assertions, dead code, unused imports.

**Second pass:** list uncommented files and ask "unrelated deletions, phantom imports,
duplicated logic, or weakened assertions?" Skip only with explicit justification.

---

## Step 3 — Consolidation

Launch one more subagent to consolidate:

1. Fetch all inline comments; keep those starting with `<!-- ai-review: -->`; parse the type.
2. Fetch PR-level comments for `<!-- ai-review:requirements -->`.
3. Group by severity: 🔒 Security → 🚨 Critical → ⚠️ Warning → 💡 Suggestion.
4. Deduplicate findings at the same `{path, line}` (±3 lines).
5. Collect one positive highlight per subagent.
6. **Gap detection:** list changed files; cross-reference against commented paths. Logic
   files with no comment go under `### 🔍 Files with no inline comments` (omit config/lock
   and pure-type files).
7. Post the summary as a PR-level comment.

**Summary format:**

```markdown
## 🤖 AI Review Summary

| | |
|---|---|
| **Subagents** | {N} (Security · Requirements · Tests · Architecture · Regression) |
| **Findings** | {N} across {M} files |

### 🔒 Security ({N})
### 🚨 Critical ({N})
### ⚠️ Warnings ({N})
### 💡 Suggestions ({N})

### 🔍 Files with no inline comments
- `path` — no findings (verify manually or re-run a targeted review)

### ✅ Highlights
- {one per subagent}

> See inline comments for detail and recommendations.
```

If nothing is found across all subagents, post "✅ No issues found across all review
dimensions." with the metadata table still included.

> Note: this review is **assistive, not a merge gate** — the required gate is CI.
